.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt NOVI-GRUBENV 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm novi-grubenv
.Nd read and write GRUB's environment block
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm path | list | create
.Nm
.Cm get Ar name
.Nm
.Cm set Ar name Ns = Ns Ar value ...
.Nm
.Cm unset Ar name ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the half of
.Nm grub-editenv
an installed Novi needs.
The GRUB userland is not on this system, so the environment block is
written here: it is a fixed 1024 bytes beside
.Pa grub.cfg ,
in GRUB's own format, and a format is not a program.
.Bl -tag -width "set name=value..."
.It Cm path
Print the block this machine uses.
.It Cm list
Print every variable in it.
.It Cm get Ar name
Print one value.
Exits 1 if it is unset.
.It Cm set Ar name Ns = Ns Ar value ...
Set one or more variables.
.It Cm unset Ar name ...
Remove one or more variables.
.It Cm create
Write an empty block.
.El
.Ss Which block
The path is derived from
.Em where grub.cfg is ,
not from
.Pa /sys/firmware/efi .
Those answer different questions: the firmware node says how this
machine booted, and what is wanted is where its GRUB reads, which is
the prefix baked into
.Pa core.img
or
.Pa bootx64.efi .
A UEFI machine whose ESP did not mount still has
.Pa /sys/firmware/efi
and has nowhere GRUB will read, so
.Nm
refuses rather than writing a block nothing reads.
.Ss What the bootloader will accept
The shipped
.Pa grub.cfg
calls
.Ic load_env Ar novi_slot ,
naming the variable.
Called bare,
.Ic load_env
imports
.Em everything
in the file into GRUB's environment,
.Va prefix
and
.Va root
included, so a block somebody appended to could redirect the
bootloader itself.
Do not remove the argument.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/boot/grub/grubenv" -compact
.It Pa /boot/grub/grubenv
.It Pa /boot/efi/EFI/BOOT/grubenv
The block, on a BIOS and a UEFI machine respectively.
.Cm path
prints whichever applies.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Boot the other slot next time:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# novi-grubenv set novi_slot=b
# reboot
.Ed
.Pp
Prefer
.Xr novi-slot 8
for that, which also checks the slot is populated.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr novi-slot 8
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC 0041.
.Sh CAVEATS
The block is 1024 bytes and every way to get the format wrong is
silent: GRUB discards a record with no terminating newline, from a
file that is the right size and looks correct in an editor.
Use
.Nm
rather than editing it.
